\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Differences on a cycle of sites}
\date{2026-11-04}


\p{Label the sites of a cycle by #{\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z}. The value of a field at
the next site is again a value at a site, and subtracting the value at a site
from the value at the next site is the difference one writes when the step has
length #{1}. The product rule a difference obeys has a correction term, and on a
cycle the last site is again the first: which rule holds when the shift wraps
around, and what does it leave uncorrected?}
